{"reference":"Psalms 133","book":"Psalms","chapter":133,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Surrounding Songs","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 133 stands within the Songs of Ascents. This surrounding collection includes communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and songs oriented toward worship. That broader setting can place the psalm’s celebration of united kinship within a collection concerned with the worshiping community, though this way of reading the collection is disputed.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 130:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_133_7e8f6e3e869e629716d3ae7e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}